<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Distributed Tracing on Nicole van der Hoeven</title><link>https://nicolevanderhoeven.com/tags/distributed-tracing/</link><description>Recent content in Distributed Tracing on Nicole van der Hoeven</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en-us</language><copyright>Nicole van der Hoeven</copyright><lastBuildDate>Fri, 19 Jan 2024 18:09:01 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://nicolevanderhoeven.com/tags/distributed-tracing/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>How to do continuous profiling right with Grafana Pyroscope and Ryan Perry, (Grafana Office Hours #26)</title><link>https://nicolevanderhoeven.com/blog/20240119-goh26-how-to-do-continuous-profiling-right-with-grafana-pyroscope/</link><pubDate>Fri, 19 Jan 2024 18:09:01 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://nicolevanderhoeven.com/blog/20240119-goh26-how-to-do-continuous-profiling-right-with-grafana-pyroscope/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;My friend &lt;a href="https://javaducky.com"&gt;Paul Balogh&lt;/a&gt; and I interview &lt;a href="https://ryanperry.io"&gt;Ryan Perry&lt;/a&gt;, co-founder of Grafana Pyroscope, about how to do continuous profiling right. Ryan, and the rest of the Pyroscope team, joined Grafana Labs, where he is now a Director of Engineer. Ryan discusses the main concerns in continuous profiling and how to avoid those pitfalls. Pyroscope is an open-source project for aggregating continuous profiling data about your system&amp;rsquo;s resources.&lt;/p&gt;
