&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item><item><title>Getting Started with OpenTelemetry (Grafana Office Hours #23)</title><link>https://nicolevanderhoeven.com/blog/20231208-goh23-getting-started-with-opentelemetry/</link><pubDate>Fri, 08 Dec 2023 17:00:23 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://nicolevanderhoeven.com/blog/20231208-goh23-getting-started-with-opentelemetry/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Principal Engineer Juraci Paixão Kröhling talks to my colleague &lt;a href="https://javaducky.com"&gt;Paul Balogh&lt;/a&gt; and me about getting started with OpenTelemetry: what it is, why everyone&amp;rsquo;s talking about it, and how to instrument your systems and improve their reliability and observability. Juraci is a contributor to open source projects like Jaeger and OpenTelemetry.&lt;/p&gt;
